WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.310
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.580 --> 00:11.310
Then why did you become a teacher?

3
00:11.310 --> 00:15.580
Isn't it because you want to become your version of an ideal teacher?

4
00:15.580 --> 00:17.350
I suppose so.

5
00:17.350 --> 00:22.890
But if I only followed my ideals, I'd never get anywhere.

6
00:22.890 --> 00:27.310
That's why I choose to accomplish the bare minimum every day.

7
00:27.310 --> 00:29.500
The bare minimum?

8
00:29.500 --> 00:33.570
To protect the lives of my students.

9
00:48.410 --> 00:51.760
You're a cool guy.

10
00:53.350 --> 00:54.640
Huh?

11
00:55.740 --> 00:57.300
You're cool.

12
00:59.990 --> 01:02.490
Cool?

13
01:02.490 --> 01:07.870
N-No, she just...

14
01:07.870 --> 01:10.200
She wouldn't get it.

15
01:10.950 --> 01:12.720
Saya.

16
01:15.990 --> 01:17.950
Saya, clean up the table.

17
01:17.950 --> 01:21.580
Okay, I'm almost done.

18
01:24.100 --> 01:27.500
How could a person from Edo understand

19
01:27.500 --> 01:30.020
the struggle of living in this modern era?

20
01:30.020 --> 01:31.970
Enough gaming.

21
01:32.690 --> 01:35.150
Set the chopsticks and cups.

22
01:35.150 --> 01:36.800
Fine.

23
01:37.940 --> 01:39.480
Where's Ms. Nashiki?

24
01:39.480 --> 01:40.750
Your room.

25
01:40.750 --> 01:43.750
- What? - She wanted to borrow a dictionary.

26
01:45.210 --> 01:46.850
Seriously?

27
01:46.850 --> 01:49.550
Ms. Nashiki, please don't barge...

28
01:53.150 --> 01:54.870
Ikuru.

29
01:55.820 --> 01:58.650
Is this all true?

30
02:01.670 --> 02:05.740
After the 15th Tokugawa shogun, their rule...

31
02:05.740 --> 02:07.620
It ends?

32
02:07.620 --> 02:10.480
Yeah.

33
02:10.480 --> 02:16.070
But Lord Tsunayoshi was just appointed the 5th shogun.

34
02:16.070 --> 02:19.600
Tsunayoshi is especially famous among the Tokugawa's.

35
02:19.600 --> 02:21.980
Why? Did something happen during his rule?

36
02:21.980 --> 02:23.400
No, nothing bad.

37
02:23.400 --> 02:25.150
Let's see... Found it.

38
02:25.150 --> 02:28.680
He enacted an effective animal welfare law.

39
02:28.680 --> 02:33.430
It punished those who brought harm onto animals, specifically dogs.

40
02:33.430 --> 02:35.580
Which is why he was called, "The Dog Shogun".

41
02:35.580 --> 02:37.200
The Dog Shogun?

42
02:37.200 --> 02:39.110
What a nasty insult!

43
02:39.110 --> 02:41.180
I see now why he's infamous.

44
02:44.250 --> 02:49.350
But my guys would've liked him. We're all dog lovers, after all.

45
02:50.250 --> 02:52.310
We had a stray that visited often.

46
02:52.310 --> 02:54.720
We called the little lad, "Mame".

47
02:54.720 --> 02:56.630
Mame!

48
02:56.630 --> 02:58.890
Nice to see you, boy!

49
02:58.890 --> 03:01.320
Come here!

50
03:01.320 --> 03:02.380
Good boy!

51
03:02.380 --> 03:04.250
How are you?

52
03:04.250 --> 03:07.950
Recently, Tsunayoshi's reputation has been re-evaluated.

53
03:07.950 --> 03:11.850
People claim his welfare laws were meant to protect all lives.

54
03:11.850 --> 03:16.300
Like modern day general welfare, it was for all who were less fortunate.

55
03:16.940 --> 03:21.000
What's most amazing though, is that this was enacted so long ago.

56
03:22.380 --> 03:26.890
He lived in an era of turmoil, where lives were less valued.

57
03:26.890 --> 03:30.600
Yet he emphasized the meaning of living, and one's life.

58
03:31.190 --> 03:33.500
I'm sure he must have had a wise advisor.

59
03:36.840 --> 03:41.200
There are plenty of intelligent folks like Lord Tsunayoshi.

60
03:41.200 --> 03:45.020
Like a mathematical genius who directly served the daimyo.

61
03:45.020 --> 03:47.030
Now he was renowned throughout Japan.

62
03:47.030 --> 03:51.030
A mathematician known all across Japan... Like Takakazu Seki?

63
03:51.030 --> 03:53.430
Wait... you know Master Seki?

64
03:53.430 --> 03:54.840
Huh? Yes.

65
03:54.840 --> 03:57.080
- What? - Hold on.

66
03:57.080 --> 03:58.410
[History of Mathematicians in Japan]

67
04:03.800 --> 04:05.660
"Takakazu Seki, Lord of Mathematics".

68
04:05.660 --> 04:07.900
Lord of Mathematics...

69
04:09.100 --> 04:13.140
Then he is being lauded as an expert?

70
04:14.330 --> 04:16.610
What a perfect title!

71
04:16.610 --> 04:19.960
So this is how Master Seki is being remembered.

72
04:19.960 --> 04:21.590
You know him?

73
04:21.590 --> 04:24.590
Yeah. He lived nearby.

74
04:24.590 --> 04:27.510
In my heart, I call him my teacher.

75
04:27.510 --> 04:28.570
He taught you?

76
04:28.570 --> 04:33.180
Of course not. He was a warrior, and I, the daughter of a commoner.

77
04:33.760 --> 04:38.890
But he is a humble and kind man.

78
04:38.890 --> 04:40.240
And...

79
04:40.240 --> 04:42.960
Mame! You're such a doll.

80
04:45.290 --> 04:47.270
So you call that dog, "Mame".

81
04:47.270 --> 04:48.680
Master Seki!

82
04:48.680 --> 04:50.080
You know of this pup?

83
04:50.080 --> 04:52.340
Indeed. He often visits my place as well.

84
04:52.340 --> 04:54.550
Though I call him, "Ritsu". (T/N: "Ratio")

85
04:54.550 --> 04:57.340
Ritsu? What an odd name.

86
04:57.340 --> 04:59.440
Sounds like a mathematical problem.

87
05:00.680 --> 05:02.310
I suppose so.

88
05:02.310 --> 05:06.950
I cannot help but think of ratios all day, and all night.

89
05:06.950 --> 05:10.780
Still, that is no reason to forget your meals.

90
05:10.780 --> 05:15.010
Ritsu, make sure to have Master Seki feed you well, alright?

91
05:17.730 --> 05:20.260
It seems I've met my match.

92
05:21.540 --> 05:23.040
Ritsu.

93
05:25.890 --> 05:27.670
How adorable.

94
05:29.340 --> 05:32.930
Ritsu, of course. What a doll!

95
05:33.510 --> 05:35.280
Ritsu.

96
05:35.280 --> 05:36.950
Are you hot?

97
05:47.390 --> 05:50.050
What're you two doing? I'm starving.

98
05:50.050 --> 05:52.150
We'll be right there.

99
05:52.150 --> 05:53.760
Sorry about that.

100
05:56.500 --> 06:00.100
What was all that about?

101
06:03.720 --> 06:06.430
That look on her face...

102
06:06.430 --> 06:08.190
This thing is so fluffy!

103
06:08.190 --> 06:10.450
But it looks like a steamed bun.

104
06:10.450 --> 06:13.160
That's called a shumai. It's good, right?

105
06:13.160 --> 06:16.050
She wasn't thinking of an acquaintance.

106
06:16.050 --> 06:18.530
How's this thing made?

107
06:18.530 --> 06:20.640
Watch a video, I'm sure it's easy.

108
06:20.640 --> 06:21.880
A video?

109
06:21.880 --> 06:26.000
She definitely harbored feelings for him.

110
06:26.000 --> 06:31.030
Ms. Nashiki had a crush on Takakazu Seki?

111
06:31.800 --> 06:34.820
Ikuru. Ikuru!

112
06:36.220 --> 06:37.440
What are you doing?

113
06:37.440 --> 06:40.630
My shumai...

114
06:41.600 --> 06:42.780
I'll go wash it off.

115
06:42.780 --> 06:45.760
Where's your mind at?

116
06:47.030 --> 06:49.260
All that sodium, it'd kill him.

117
07:05.770 --> 07:07.290
Woah!

118
07:07.290 --> 07:09.600
They finished cooking in an instant.

119
07:09.600 --> 07:12.220
Only because they edited the video.

120
07:12.220 --> 07:13.410
"Edited"?

121
07:13.410 --> 07:16.560
Anyway, they're telling you it's practically this easy.

122
07:16.560 --> 07:18.920
I see.

123
07:18.920 --> 07:23.470
This thing called a "smartphone" is quite the contraption.

124
07:23.470 --> 07:25.490
Yeah. You can look up anything.

125
07:25.490 --> 07:29.920
All thanks to the World Wide Web. [Rinka Saeki]

126
07:29.920 --> 07:31.940
Ikuru. [Rinka Saeki]

127
07:31.940 --> 07:34.660
You better come today.

128
07:34.660 --> 07:36.740
I'll be waiting until you arrive.

129
07:37.600 --> 07:40.110
- Ikuru. - Huh?

130
07:40.110 --> 07:42.820
Does that mean we won't be needed one day?

131
07:44.090 --> 07:49.010
Like couriers, will teachers become unnecessary, too?

132
07:50.830 --> 07:53.200
- Of course not. - Really?

133
07:53.200 --> 07:56.410
Less people want to become teachers. It's possible.

134
07:56.410 --> 08:00.310
Dummy. Teachers teach more than just textbook knowledge.

135
08:02.980 --> 08:05.800
Same goes for Edo period teachers, right?

136
08:09.370 --> 08:11.450
You're right.

137
08:20.910 --> 08:23.990
[Episode 3]

138
08:23.990 --> 08:27.800
[Narita Airport Terminal 1]

139
08:39.240 --> 08:45.400
Pathetic as I may be, I have been told I was liked once.

140
08:45.400 --> 08:49.470
And what year was he appointed? Saeki.

141
08:50.300 --> 08:53.400
Hey. Saeki.

142
08:53.400 --> 08:56.220
Rinka. Rinka, wake up!

143
08:56.220 --> 08:59.610
Saeki. Wake up!

144
09:02.150 --> 09:05.300
Is my class that boring to you?

145
09:07.590 --> 09:09.140
Out in the hall!

146
09:12.060 --> 09:13.670
What?

147
09:18.710 --> 09:20.850
Sir.

148
09:20.850 --> 09:22.180
What?

149
09:23.290 --> 09:26.040
You should file a divorce already.

150
09:26.040 --> 09:28.590
I think your relationship is far beyond repair.

151
09:30.440 --> 09:32.530
Settle down!

152
09:37.570 --> 09:40.430
Rinka, class is over.

153
09:53.250 --> 09:55.510
Damn it...

154
09:57.170 --> 09:59.140
I'm so unlucky.

155
09:59.140 --> 10:01.000
No.

156
10:01.000 --> 10:02.950
You're super lucky.

157
10:04.140 --> 10:07.140
You shouldn't mess with our teacher like that.

158
10:07.140 --> 10:08.800
Why not?

159
10:08.800 --> 10:10.890
I was only telling him the truth.

160
10:10.890 --> 10:13.220
The truth?

161
10:13.220 --> 10:16.880
His shirt collar was a bit dirty.

162
10:16.880 --> 10:20.240
I bet his wife isn't doing laundry for him.

163
10:20.240 --> 10:22.640
And I saw he hired a private detective.

164
10:22.640 --> 10:25.170
That already proves their relationship is over.

165
10:25.170 --> 10:26.910
Who are you, Sherlock Holmes?

166
10:26.910 --> 10:29.530
You saw how angry he was.

167
10:29.530 --> 10:31.960
I'd never want to marry a guy like him.

168
10:31.960 --> 10:35.860
That's just your opinion.

169
10:35.860 --> 10:37.900
Fair enough.

170
10:40.070 --> 10:42.680
Keep this up, and you'll never make friends.

171
10:42.680 --> 10:44.490
I don't need friends.

172
10:44.490 --> 10:47.000
And it's not like anyone's bullying me.

173
10:47.000 --> 10:51.410
Besides, observing people is exhausting enough.

174
10:51.920 --> 10:55.700
As your parent, I worry about you.

175
10:55.700 --> 10:57.150
- My parent? - Yeah.

176
10:57.150 --> 10:59.010
You?

177
10:59.010 --> 11:02.640
You grew attached to me like a baby bird, remember?

178
11:02.640 --> 11:04.740
Wait.

179
11:18.300 --> 11:20.200
Let's go home.

180
11:23.940 --> 11:25.180
Okay!

181
11:27.000 --> 11:30.960
What, you think I'm a baby chick?

182
11:31.700 --> 11:34.540
Well, I won't deny it.

183
11:39.870 --> 11:42.330
- I like you. - Huh?

184
11:42.330 --> 11:45.740
Your unluckiness, that is.

185
11:46.230 --> 11:49.580
You never blame others for something bad happening,

186
11:49.580 --> 11:51.540
nor hate them for it.

187
11:51.540 --> 11:55.030
And you have this refreshing, clear aura about you.

188
11:55.030 --> 11:58.600
You're not making any sense.

189
11:58.600 --> 12:00.620
What?

190
12:00.620 --> 12:03.210
I'm taking a nap. Night!

191
12:08.350 --> 12:10.040
Rinka!

192
12:16.710 --> 12:18.320
You're late.

193
12:19.110 --> 12:20.350
Don't call me out here without warning.

194
12:20.350 --> 12:24.290
Why not? You don't have anyone else anyway.

195
12:24.290 --> 12:25.680
Huh?

196
12:27.760 --> 12:31.100
I have Saya, and my job.

197
12:31.100 --> 12:35.580
So, today's the day, right? We gotta do it.

198
12:35.580 --> 12:38.950
Okay, here goes. Come here.

199
12:43.880 --> 12:45.810
What time is your flight?

200
12:45.810 --> 12:48.290
- Are you going to Europe again? - China.

201
12:48.290 --> 12:50.960
I'll be competing at the WGOP.

202
12:50.960 --> 12:52.000
What's that?

203
12:52.000 --> 12:56.160
The World Grand Prix of Poker.

204
12:56.160 --> 13:00.650
Win this, and I'll be the poker world champ.

205
13:00.650 --> 13:02.390
How much is the prize pool?

206
13:02.390 --> 13:05.560
- Several hundreds of millions. - Woah.

207
13:05.560 --> 13:08.710
Then go become the champ already.

208
13:11.410 --> 13:12.850
Come here.

209
13:17.240 --> 13:20.610
Hurry up, you're embarrasing me.

210
13:21.330 --> 13:22.680
Bring it in.

211
13:24.150 --> 13:26.010
Is this what you want?

212
13:34.130 --> 13:35.750
Hurry up.

213
13:44.900 --> 13:48.450
Are you sure this will help?

214
13:50.130 --> 13:51.560
Yup.

215
13:53.200 --> 13:54.560
Thanks.

216
13:54.560 --> 13:55.950
Sure.

217
13:56.940 --> 13:58.450
See you.

218
14:01.260 --> 14:02.920
Good luck.

219
14:02.920 --> 14:04.420
Yeah.

220
14:07.110 --> 14:08.240
Bet.

221
14:08.240 --> 14:09.230
All in.

222
14:09.230 --> 14:10.690
All in.

223
14:13.070 --> 14:14.250
Call.

224
14:14.250 --> 14:15.550
All in, called.

225
14:15.550 --> 14:18.010
King.

226
14:20.890 --> 14:24.000
If anyone found out, they'd die of laughter.

227
14:24.000 --> 14:27.030
To think this is your good luck routine.

228
14:29.910 --> 14:31.760
Actually, never mind.

229
14:31.760 --> 14:33.110
Huh?

230
14:37.500 --> 14:39.510
You have someone else, don't you?

231
14:40.240 --> 14:43.070
- Huh? - Your heart rate increased.

232
14:43.070 --> 14:45.580
N-No? No, no, no!

233
14:45.580 --> 14:47.400
I knew it.

234
14:47.400 --> 14:51.390
There's someone else you're interested in.

235
14:52.350 --> 14:56.260
I thought I was the only one who had you at their whims.

236
14:56.260 --> 14:58.000
But I guess that's not true anymore?

237
14:58.000 --> 14:59.680
What are you talking about?

238
14:59.680 --> 15:02.010
This is an important competition, right?

239
15:02.010 --> 15:03.100
Come on, bring it in.

240
15:03.100 --> 15:06.810
You don't need to act like my parent anymore.

241
15:10.420 --> 15:13.040
We've known each other for a long time now,

242
15:13.040 --> 15:15.780
but our routine was the oddity.

243
15:16.590 --> 15:20.740
We got too comfortable with our relationship, didn't we?

244
15:22.070 --> 15:24.030
Well...

245
15:24.930 --> 15:26.690
I guess so.

246
15:27.670 --> 15:32.050
We got too comfortable with our routine.

247
15:33.780 --> 15:38.680
We're only childhood friends, yet I thought I was so special.

248
15:38.680 --> 15:40.310
I'm...

249
15:42.720 --> 15:44.150
I'm sorry.

250
15:45.490 --> 15:48.010
And if I said I'd forgive you?

251
15:48.550 --> 15:51.960
I'll forgive you, Ikuru.

252
15:51.960 --> 15:54.460
If you're honest with me.

253
15:54.460 --> 15:56.710
Honest?

254
15:58.880 --> 16:03.200
Who's on your mind right now?

255
16:33.510 --> 16:35.980
Your heart rate's gotten even quicker.

256
16:39.440 --> 16:41.660
Of course it would.

257
16:41.660 --> 16:44.000
Then I've successfully overwritten them.

258
16:44.640 --> 16:49.210
I'll win and be right back, so wait for me, okay?

259
16:56.450 --> 16:59.200
I thought that was going to be my first!

260
17:00.110 --> 17:01.650
What's going on?

261
17:01.650 --> 17:03.130
What was all that about?

262
17:03.130 --> 17:06.360
Was she teasing me? Or being serious?

263
17:07.220 --> 17:10.800
Am I finally graduating from childhood friend,

264
17:10.800 --> 17:14.340
to boyfriend status?

265
17:31.850 --> 17:35.180
You scared me.

266
17:35.180 --> 17:36.410
Welcome back.

267
17:36.410 --> 17:38.980
I have returned home.

268
17:39.620 --> 17:41.940
Why do I feel guilty?

269
17:41.940 --> 17:44.140
Your hair is wet. Use the hairdryer.

270
17:44.140 --> 17:46.740
What a pain. I'll let it air dry.

271
17:46.740 --> 17:48.680
If you don't blow dry it, you'll wake up with cowlicks,

272
17:48.680 --> 17:50.360
and create more trouble for yourself.

273
17:50.360 --> 17:54.500
Those little troubles, build up into a huge pain.

274
17:54.500 --> 17:55.820
So here.

275
17:55.820 --> 17:56.780
What're you talking about?

276
17:56.780 --> 17:59.870
I'm speaking common sense here.

277
17:59.870 --> 18:02.100
Like a nagging sister-in-law.

278
18:02.100 --> 18:03.780
Night.

279
18:03.780 --> 18:05.400
What?

280
18:06.740 --> 18:10.360
Who's on your mind right now?

281
18:11.070 --> 18:14.570
That's actually a great question.

282
18:15.070 --> 18:18.800
Who is on my mind right now?

283
18:20.750 --> 18:24.430
Who... Or rather, which one?

284
18:26.420 --> 18:29.570
No, what do you mean, which one?

285
18:31.780 --> 18:33.840
Why are you so spooked?

286
18:33.840 --> 18:35.810
I changed my mind.

287
18:42.720 --> 18:43.680
[Teacher's Office]

288
18:43.680 --> 18:46.700
- Morning. - I'm so sleepy.

289
18:46.700 --> 18:48.720
How many days until summer vacation?

290
18:48.720 --> 18:51.040
One, two... Agh, the Sports Festival.

291
18:51.040 --> 18:54.000
'Tis the season, again.

292
18:54.000 --> 18:56.060
- Good morning. - Good morning.

293
18:56.060 --> 18:59.000
Tea is served, folks.

294
18:59.000 --> 19:00.340
Hey, what are you doing?

295
19:00.340 --> 19:02.650
I don't know whose cup is whose...

296
19:02.650 --> 19:06.070
You brewed us tea, Ms. Nashiki?

297
19:06.070 --> 19:07.200
Yes, sir.

298
19:07.200 --> 19:10.090
The electric kettle's an amazing invention.

299
19:10.090 --> 19:14.040
The water boils without any fire! Right?

300
19:14.040 --> 19:15.980
- Right... - Ms. Nashiki.

301
19:15.980 --> 19:18.850
Are you doing this out of obligation?

302
19:18.850 --> 19:22.030
- Obligation? - Are you all thirsty?

303
19:22.030 --> 19:24.030
- Miss! Thanks a million. - Thank you.

304
19:24.030 --> 19:25.560
- Careful, it's hot. - Thanks.

305
19:25.560 --> 19:27.500
Don't burn yourselves.

306
19:28.430 --> 19:31.540
Tea's ready.

307
19:31.540 --> 19:34.960
Come get some. Careful!

308
19:35.660 --> 19:37.190
No obligation at all.

309
19:37.190 --> 19:38.800
Now here, have some.

310
19:38.800 --> 19:40.810
- Thank you. - Sure.

311
19:40.810 --> 19:42.620
- I appreciate it. - No problem.

312
19:42.620 --> 19:43.810
Ms. Akutsu, here.

313
19:43.810 --> 19:47.080
Excuse me. Here you go.

314
19:48.430 --> 19:51.350
Come and get your tea!

315
19:51.350 --> 19:53.020
Tea is great on Monday mornings.

316
19:53.020 --> 19:55.070
- Agreed. - Thank you.

317
19:55.070 --> 19:56.640
Of course.

318
19:56.640 --> 19:58.160
- Ms. Nashiki. - Yes?

319
19:58.160 --> 20:01.280
You have my cup there.

320
20:01.280 --> 20:03.140
- Which one? - That one there.

321
20:03.140 --> 20:05.660
Ah, this one! Here you go.

322
20:05.660 --> 20:07.750
Oh my.

323
20:07.750 --> 20:11.590
My tea leaf is upright. Look here.

324
20:11.590 --> 20:14.180
- What a great sign! - It's a first for me.

325
20:14.180 --> 20:15.380
Today's your lucky day.

326
20:15.380 --> 20:17.360
Really? Goodness.

327
20:17.360 --> 20:19.860
It must be because you brewed it.

328
20:19.860 --> 20:22.420
- You think so? - Thank you.

329
20:22.420 --> 20:24.520
Of course.

330
20:24.520 --> 20:28.030
Who else... Is this yours?

331
20:28.030 --> 20:30.070
- Yes, thank you. - Sure thing.

332
20:30.070 --> 20:34.060
Who's left? This is a fine cup.

333
20:34.060 --> 20:35.330
Huh?

334
20:35.330 --> 20:36.380
That one would be mine.

335
20:36.380 --> 20:38.460
Ms. Principal!

336
20:38.460 --> 20:41.300
- You have excellent taste. - My!

337
20:41.300 --> 20:42.550
- Thank you. - I shall carry it in.

338
20:42.550 --> 20:45.820
- Why, thank you. - Of course.

339
20:47.160 --> 20:50.070
Do I have to do that too?

340
20:50.070 --> 20:51.990
No.

341
20:58.210 --> 21:00.960
Damn it.

342
21:00.960 --> 21:03.140
Why did she brew them tea?

343
21:03.140 --> 21:07.990
She's going to make tea serving a job for us women, again.

344
21:07.990 --> 21:11.330
The rights we fought for will go down the drain!

345
21:11.330 --> 21:14.200
It's just tea. Get it yourselves, you know?

346
21:14.200 --> 21:15.330
Exactly.

347
21:15.330 --> 21:20.340
- Those men when they get tea... - They look so full of themselves.

348
21:20.340 --> 21:23.280
What's so wrong about serving tea?

349
21:23.280 --> 21:26.970
I didn't see anything about that on the manual...

350
21:32.120 --> 21:34.830
[Become a proper teacher at my own pace]

351
21:44.020 --> 21:45.580
[Math]

352
22:07.920 --> 22:10.440
Everyone ready for the science quiz?

353
22:10.440 --> 22:12.860
Yes, Mr. Majima.

354
22:12.860 --> 22:15.190
Then please log in to your tablets.

355
22:15.190 --> 22:17.110
Okay.

356
22:18.330 --> 22:20.900
- I've logged in. - Me too.

357
22:20.900 --> 22:22.720
Everyone ready?

358
22:22.720 --> 22:24.540
Mr. Majima.

359
22:24.540 --> 22:27.270
Naoya's not logged in yet.

360
22:29.850 --> 22:31.960
Everyone else, start on your quizzes.

361
22:31.960 --> 22:33.830
I'll set the timer to 10 minutes.

362
22:33.830 --> 22:36.360
Ready? Begin.

363
22:41.570 --> 22:44.390
Sano, you need to learn how to navigate the tablet.

364
22:44.390 --> 22:47.310
- Yes, Mr. Majima. - Remember, first you click here to login.

365
22:47.310 --> 22:49.250
Do you know your ID?

366
22:49.250 --> 22:51.630
- No. - Okay.

367
22:51.630 --> 22:53.690
Let's see...

368
22:53.690 --> 22:58.670
Points will be docked off for incorrect strokes.

369
22:59.400 --> 23:01.530
Remember, I can see your overall percentile,

370
23:01.530 --> 23:04.300
and time it took for you all to answer.

371
23:04.960 --> 23:07.200
And one more reminder.

372
23:07.200 --> 23:11.850
I can see your search histories as well.

373
23:14.040 --> 23:16.140
I will repeat.

374
23:16.700 --> 23:20.220
I am able to see your search history.

375
23:20.220 --> 23:22.990
Alright, settle down.

376
23:26.150 --> 23:30.070
It's time for mathematics... I mean, math.

377
23:30.070 --> 23:31.520
Yes, Ms. Nashiki.

378
23:31.520 --> 23:33.600
Get seated.

379
23:34.230 --> 23:38.660
Oh, uh... we don't need those tablet thingies.

380
23:38.660 --> 23:40.610
What?

381
23:40.610 --> 23:43.480
We won't be using our tablets?

382
23:43.480 --> 23:48.170
Nope. Today, we'll be getting to know this lad here.

383
23:48.780 --> 23:50.030
An oval!

384
23:50.030 --> 23:53.480
No, that's a circle.

385
23:53.480 --> 23:55.590
Good answer.

386
23:55.590 --> 23:57.480
An oval...

387
23:58.000 --> 24:02.920
Could be drawn like this, or this, and still be an oval.

388
24:03.770 --> 24:08.240
But in mathematics... math,

389
24:08.240 --> 24:15.240
a circle is made up of points, that are from a given center.

390
24:16.020 --> 24:17.920
The center.

391
24:17.920 --> 24:19.650
The radius.

392
24:19.650 --> 24:21.900
The diameter.

393
24:21.900 --> 24:23.500
The circumference.

394
24:23.500 --> 24:26.960
Many things make up a circle.

395
24:26.960 --> 24:30.170
Today, we will be getting to know what makes a circle.

396
24:30.170 --> 24:31.470
Yes, Ms. Nashiki.

397
24:31.470 --> 24:35.480
First, let's try to find the area of a circle.

398
24:35.480 --> 24:37.360
What?

399
24:37.360 --> 24:41.160
You're free to cut, fold, or do whatever with the circle.

400
24:41.160 --> 24:43.490
Let's brainstorm how to find this area.

401
24:43.490 --> 24:46.360
- I'm allowed to cut it? - Of course.

402
24:46.360 --> 24:49.570
Ms. Nashiki, let's just use our tablets.

403
24:49.570 --> 24:51.370
I already learned this in cram school.

404
24:51.370 --> 24:53.550
So did I.

405
24:53.550 --> 24:56.030
See, look at my tablet.

406
24:56.030 --> 25:01.200
The area of a circle is found by multiplying the radius with itself, and 3.14.

407
25:02.880 --> 25:08.400
The ratio of a circle's circumference to its diameter, is 3.14!

408
25:22.270 --> 25:26.200
Master Seki, is this the "ratio" you spoke of?

409
25:26.200 --> 25:30.580
Indeed. I was searching for a way to accurately measure the area of a circle.

410
25:30.580 --> 25:37.480
I started by hypothesizing a polygon that would be closest to a circle.

411
25:37.480 --> 25:39.710
A polygon, close to a circle.

412
25:39.710 --> 25:44.250
In theory, the area of this polygon would also give me the area of the circle.

413
25:44.250 --> 25:45.630
I see.

414
25:45.630 --> 25:49.370
How many sides of this hypothetical polygon have you calculated thus far?

415
25:50.400 --> 25:55.820
I've currently calculated 131,072 sides.

416
25:55.820 --> 26:01.000
131,072 sides?

417
26:01.000 --> 26:04.640
This calculation has brought me to a certain equation.

418
26:06.210 --> 26:08.990
If you multiply the diameter of a circle to a certain number,

419
26:08.990 --> 26:10.380
you get its area.

420
26:10.380 --> 26:12.440
Such a number exists?

421
26:12.440 --> 26:16.250
I've calculated up to 11 digits of this number thus far.

422
26:16.250 --> 26:21.650
The number being, 3.14159265359.

423
26:21.650 --> 26:25.670
Huh? What? 3.1415...

424
26:25.670 --> 26:30.070
If you only want an approximation of the area, 3.14 will do.

425
26:30.700 --> 26:36.890
I have decided to call this number, the circumference ratio.

426
26:36.890 --> 26:39.440
The circumference ratio...

427
26:40.450 --> 26:43.510
3.14...

428
26:44.640 --> 26:46.850
I know about 3.14, too.

429
26:46.850 --> 26:49.000
- So do I! - Me too!

430
27:09.720 --> 27:12.060
Ms. Nashiki, what's wrong?

431
27:12.060 --> 27:15.350
Do you not know about 3.14?

432
27:15.350 --> 27:17.330
Ms. Nashiki?

433
27:17.330 --> 27:19.840
No, I do.

434
27:25.700 --> 27:31.380
This number is very important to me.

435
27:31.900 --> 27:37.160
It was a number discovered through perseverance and effort

436
27:37.160 --> 27:39.970
by my very own teacher.

437
27:40.570 --> 27:47.140
That's why I want you all to puzzle out how to find the area, alright?

438
27:47.140 --> 27:49.150
Yes, Ms. Nashiki!

439
27:57.240 --> 27:59.980
My dad bought me a Switch 2!

440
27:59.980 --> 28:01.630
- What? - Lucky!

441
28:01.630 --> 28:02.840
Awesome, right?

442
28:02.840 --> 28:05.440
Does anyone know how to use commands in Minecraft?

443
28:05.440 --> 28:08.230
I do! I can spawn items even in a desert.

444
28:08.230 --> 28:10.320
- Seriously? - That's sick!

445
28:10.320 --> 28:11.540
I made a friend on Roblox, too.

446
28:11.540 --> 28:13.180
So who's coming over today?

447
28:13.180 --> 28:16.310
- Me! - Me too!

448
28:16.310 --> 28:18.160
You coming too, Naoya?

449
28:19.860 --> 28:21.330
Of course you aren't!

450
28:21.330 --> 28:25.410
You can't login, or even play Mario Kart!

451
28:26.570 --> 28:30.250
Come on, let's go!

452
28:45.440 --> 28:48.110
That looks great!

453
28:48.110 --> 28:50.220
You got an interesting pattern there.

454
28:50.790 --> 28:52.000
I see you're making it look cool.

455
28:52.000 --> 28:53.550
I'm gonna try attaching this to it.

456
28:53.550 --> 28:56.630
Sounds good.

457
28:56.630 --> 28:58.430
Ms. Nashiki, look! Flowers!

458
28:58.430 --> 29:00.630
- They're looking real pretty. - It's cute!

459
29:00.630 --> 29:02.120
Right?

460
29:02.120 --> 29:05.610
Ms. Nashiki, look!

461
29:05.610 --> 29:07.040
Yeah, that's a big one.

462
29:07.040 --> 29:10.600
Ms. Nashiki, look at mine!

463
29:10.600 --> 29:13.340
What're you guys making?

464
29:13.340 --> 29:16.740
I see. Looks interesting.

465
29:16.740 --> 29:19.110
Ms. Nashiki. Ryota's messing around.

466
29:19.110 --> 29:20.310
He cut his all up.

467
29:20.310 --> 29:23.000
I'm just making pizza! See?

468
29:23.000 --> 29:25.460
This side is mayo-corn, and this side is teriyaki.

469
29:25.460 --> 29:26.980
Pizza? I want a slice!

470
29:26.980 --> 29:28.320
Pizza?

471
29:28.320 --> 29:31.900
I cut a slice for everyone.

472
29:33.460 --> 29:36.300
Ms. Nashiki, this is a waste of time.

473
29:36.300 --> 29:40.440
I want to do a normal class, not this.

474
29:40.440 --> 29:44.510
But Minato, Yuzuki. Look.

475
29:44.510 --> 29:48.200
Ryota just discovered the true nature of a circle.

476
29:48.200 --> 29:50.470
Huh? I did?

477
29:50.470 --> 29:53.300
This is what makes circles so interesting.

478
29:53.300 --> 29:55.190
Watch.

479
29:55.190 --> 30:01.180
If you take this "pizza", and line up the pieces

480
30:01.180 --> 30:03.190
like so...

481
30:03.190 --> 30:06.910
Keep watching.

482
30:08.010 --> 30:09.740
What's it making?

483
30:11.080 --> 30:13.500
I'll keep stacking.

484
30:13.500 --> 30:15.140
See? What's that?

485
30:15.140 --> 30:17.760
Hey, it became a long rectangle.

486
30:17.760 --> 30:20.710
- You're right. - A rectangle!

487
30:20.710 --> 30:22.200
Does that mean...

488
30:22.200 --> 30:27.370
The height of a parallelogram is a circle's radius?

489
30:28.200 --> 30:31.200
Ryota, isn't Math fun?

490
30:31.200 --> 30:32.300
Yeah!

491
30:32.300 --> 30:34.920
- That's so interesting! - No way!

492
30:43.950 --> 30:45.830
["Please"]

493
30:45.830 --> 30:47.070
Good work.

494
30:47.070 --> 30:48.970
Likewise.

495
30:51.030 --> 30:52.600
Ms. Nashiki.

496
30:52.600 --> 30:54.720
Mr. Majima?

497
30:54.720 --> 30:58.320
As a fellow third grade teacher, I raise issue with your methods!

498
30:59.510 --> 31:05.020
You haven't used tablets in your class once since we returned from break.

499
31:05.600 --> 31:07.710
- Right... - Ms. Nashiki.

500
31:07.710 --> 31:09.480
What are you doing?

501
31:09.480 --> 31:13.810
Do you plan to ignore the Ministry's GIGA Schooling Curriculum?

502
31:13.810 --> 31:16.140
This curriculum is mandated by the nation.

503
31:16.140 --> 31:20.530
They've invested hundreds of millions of yen to teach our kids about ICT.

504
31:21.090 --> 31:25.220
Taxpaying money is used to nurture the future of these children.

505
31:25.220 --> 31:27.200
But you...

506
31:28.100 --> 31:30.000
Because of your methods...

507
31:32.580 --> 31:34.660
Sano, what are you doing?

508
31:36.100 --> 31:37.330
Hey!

509
31:37.850 --> 31:41.150
- Are you okay? - Are you okay?

510
31:42.150 --> 31:44.680
Knock it off, Sano.

511
31:44.680 --> 31:46.990
You're causing trouble for your classmates!

512
31:48.040 --> 31:50.360
Then kick me out!

513
31:50.360 --> 31:53.600
Mr. Majima, I'll leave Class 1.

514
31:53.600 --> 31:56.190
I wanna go to Class 3 instead!

515
31:56.190 --> 31:57.270
Class 3?

516
31:57.270 --> 31:59.880
Please, let me go to Class 3.

517
31:59.880 --> 32:02.710
I wanna join Ms. Nashiki's class!

518
32:05.180 --> 32:08.660
We are following proper guidance when giving our lessons.

519
32:08.660 --> 32:12.380
If you ignore the rules, it will cause trouble in the other classes,

520
32:12.380 --> 32:14.340
do you understand that?

521
32:17.240 --> 32:21.520
He makes a point. Class 3 has been quite loud recently.

522
32:21.520 --> 32:24.770
You use the library, and have them move desks during lessons.

523
32:24.770 --> 32:27.970
But they're learning!

524
32:27.970 --> 32:29.810
Ms. Nashiki.

525
32:30.640 --> 32:34.320
You are hindering the future of these youth.

526
32:34.320 --> 32:38.810
If you continue with your ways, your kids will become the underdogs.

527
32:39.500 --> 32:41.370
Underdogs?

528
32:43.050 --> 32:45.660
All my students have learned.

529
32:45.660 --> 32:48.430
Today, we studied the essence of a circle.

530
32:48.430 --> 32:52.830
Essence? Just have them look it up on their tablets.

531
32:52.830 --> 32:56.530
Videos, apps, many things can teach them that.

532
32:56.530 --> 32:59.370
You must use their time efficiently.

533
32:59.370 --> 33:00.930
Exactly.

534
33:00.930 --> 33:03.020
You are disregarding your responsibility as a teacher!

535
33:03.020 --> 33:04.550
Mr. Majima, Ms. Nashiki...

536
33:04.550 --> 33:07.010
Disregarding my responsibility?

537
33:08.300 --> 33:10.980
I don't get a word you're saying.

538
33:10.980 --> 33:13.050
- Pardon? - I mean,

539
33:13.050 --> 33:16.740
my students discovered for themselves what makes a circle.

540
33:16.740 --> 33:19.050
They won't forget this experience for life.

541
33:19.050 --> 33:24.680
But criticizing my methods, because I won't use these "tools"?

542
33:24.680 --> 33:27.170
That's not what teaching is about.

543
33:27.170 --> 33:30.100
Studying and the use of tools are separate lessons to learn.

544
33:30.100 --> 33:34.530
Is it really our jobs to teach them how to use these tools?

545
33:34.530 --> 33:38.040
These children are born as digital natives.

546
33:38.040 --> 33:40.330
Tablets will continue to be a part of their lives.

547
33:40.330 --> 33:43.250
They have to know how to use this technology!

548
33:43.250 --> 33:47.280
But is it really our job as teachers to teach them that?

549
33:47.280 --> 33:52.730
Aren't teachers supposed to teach kids how to think through problems?

550
33:55.850 --> 33:58.490
Their time is limited, right?

551
33:58.490 --> 34:03.020
Then we ought to teach them how to study.

552
34:03.900 --> 34:07.180
Even so, this is something we have to teach them.

553
34:09.170 --> 34:11.350
Tablets are merely tools.

554
34:11.350 --> 34:13.240
You're right about that.

555
34:13.240 --> 34:15.960
But knowing how to use tech is the norm now.

556
34:15.960 --> 34:19.300
And if you can't, then you're looked down on.

557
34:19.300 --> 34:21.500
That's the reality we live in.

558
34:22.040 --> 34:26.230
But these tools are very expensive.

559
34:26.230 --> 34:30.200
Tablets, game consoles - not every household can afford them.

560
34:30.200 --> 34:34.950
So these opportunities at school may be their only chance to acclimate.

561
34:36.930 --> 34:43.000
By utilizing these tools, kids may even discover new talents.

562
34:43.910 --> 34:48.240
It's not only textbook knowledge we teach, right?

563
34:51.800 --> 34:53.860
Wow...

564
34:53.860 --> 34:56.740
Everyone's already adapted to using 3.14.

565
34:56.740 --> 35:02.680
Indeed. The number I discovered has become but a tool to my pupils.

566
35:04.010 --> 35:06.210
Master Seki...

567
35:06.210 --> 35:08.160
How can you smile about such a thing?

568
35:08.160 --> 35:10.410
If it were me, I would feel vexed.

569
35:10.410 --> 35:11.380
Oh?

570
35:11.380 --> 35:14.460
I mean, you worked so hard to reach the number 3.14...

571
35:14.460 --> 35:15.880
Quite stingy, aren't you?

572
35:15.880 --> 35:17.090
Oh, shush.

573
35:17.090 --> 35:21.250
It doesn't really matter who discovered the number.

574
35:21.250 --> 35:26.210
For my goals lie much higher than this.

575
35:31.510 --> 35:33.300
The circumference ratio.

576
35:33.300 --> 35:35.910
Only this number will be passed on,

577
35:35.910 --> 35:38.420
like a handy tool to utilize.

578
35:38.420 --> 35:40.570
What do you think happens next?

579
35:41.310 --> 35:47.150
This number will continue supporting people for generations to come.

580
35:48.580 --> 35:54.600
Even if our names fade into obscurity.

581
35:56.720 --> 36:01.170
It shall become a tool anyone can use.

582
36:02.600 --> 36:06.030
A tool, passed into the future.

583
36:12.480 --> 36:14.820
A tool used right

584
36:16.360 --> 36:19.800
can help a child learn.

585
36:25.670 --> 36:28.480
Mr. Majima, Ms. Akutsu.

586
36:29.110 --> 36:31.140
I'm so sorry.

587
36:31.140 --> 36:33.530
My thinking was shallow and foolish.

588
36:33.530 --> 36:35.410
Ms. Nashiki?

589
36:36.320 --> 36:41.160
You two both spoke of lessons necessary for this era.

590
36:41.160 --> 36:42.230
No, I...

591
36:42.230 --> 36:46.330
I am truly sorry to you both.

592
36:47.150 --> 36:51.620
Goodness, I can't with this...

593
36:53.310 --> 36:55.120
What's going on?

594
36:55.120 --> 36:59.300
- Has there been a fight? - No, ma'am.

595
36:59.300 --> 37:03.140
Mr. Majima, did you make Ms. Nashiki cry?

596
37:03.140 --> 37:04.590
No, I...

597
37:04.590 --> 37:06.640
Ms. Principal, this was because...

598
37:06.640 --> 37:11.850
I don't know what happened, but making her apologize here?

599
37:11.850 --> 37:14.580
I'd consider that workplace harassment.

600
37:14.580 --> 37:17.210
No, erm...

601
37:17.210 --> 37:22.550
I am not giving you a warning. Just some friendly advice.

602
37:22.550 --> 37:24.600
Ms. Principal, you misunderstand.

603
37:24.600 --> 37:28.920
These two were only teaching me something important.

604
37:28.920 --> 37:32.460
I was apologizing for my ignorance.

605
37:32.460 --> 37:34.820
I'm sorry you all had to watch.

606
37:34.820 --> 37:36.830
And I apologize for the ruckus.

607
37:37.640 --> 37:39.240
I see.

608
37:39.240 --> 37:42.020
- Then nothing happened? - Yes, ma'am.

609
37:43.710 --> 37:46.230
Then I'll let this slide.

610
37:47.660 --> 37:49.970
Talk to me if you need anything.

611
37:49.970 --> 37:53.150
So, what should we tell the Ministry?

612
37:53.150 --> 37:54.600
Right, the Ministry.

613
37:54.600 --> 37:56.050
Sorry.

614
37:56.620 --> 37:59.340
Alright, let's leave it at that.

615
37:59.340 --> 38:01.380
Everyone back to work.

616
38:43.500 --> 38:48.200
Even if our names fade into obscurity.

617
38:49.020 --> 38:52.470
It will become a tool, passed into the future.

618
38:54.020 --> 38:56.010
Master Seki...

619
38:57.150 --> 38:59.740
You're amazing, Master Seki.

620
38:59.740 --> 39:03.020
You always look far towards the future.

621
39:03.020 --> 39:06.570
Yet you seem to forget every meal.

622
39:07.920 --> 39:11.170
Only you scold me, Iroha.

623
39:11.170 --> 39:13.190
Isn't that right, Ritsu?

624
39:19.540 --> 39:22.110
Why couldn't I be a wrestler?

625
39:22.930 --> 39:24.670
What do you mean?

626
39:24.670 --> 39:29.300
If not a wrestler, then a master swordsman.

627
39:29.300 --> 39:31.680
Or even a ninja.

628
39:32.280 --> 39:35.810
Then I could have protected you.

629
39:38.620 --> 39:41.120
While you take on an important job,

630
39:41.120 --> 39:43.980
I would always protect you at your side,

631
39:43.980 --> 39:46.800
whether it rains droplets or spears.

632
39:46.800 --> 39:48.180
Isn't that right?

633
39:49.990 --> 39:52.050
You already protect me plenty.

634
39:52.050 --> 39:54.350
Is that good?

635
39:54.350 --> 39:55.820
You're a speedy eater.

636
39:58.460 --> 40:02.380
I have sometimes hoped you were instead born to a warrior family.

637
40:03.840 --> 40:08.480
After all, I have a duty of continuing my family lineage.

638
40:11.210 --> 40:14.740
What do you...

639
40:14.740 --> 40:18.820
Mathematics is my priority.

640
40:19.570 --> 40:22.830
As such, I offer myself wholly to the god of mathematics.

641
40:24.180 --> 40:26.840
I believe whoever I am to wed

642
40:28.050 --> 40:30.100
will feel quite lonesome as a result.

643
40:30.820 --> 40:32.620
No.

644
40:33.840 --> 40:35.570
If it were me, I would never...

645
40:35.570 --> 40:38.080
But you are the daughter of a commoner.

646
40:39.840 --> 40:43.760
An eccentric one, who has a passion for mathematics.

647
40:45.120 --> 40:49.440
That fact itself made me overjoyed.

648
40:50.790 --> 40:54.620
For it meant we could be together forever.

649
40:56.380 --> 41:00.010
No one can predict the events that are to come.

650
41:01.070 --> 41:04.590
And as a warrior, I must obey my orders.

651
41:06.360 --> 41:08.000
However...

652
41:09.380 --> 41:14.120
Iroha, thanks to mathematics, we are connected,

653
41:14.120 --> 41:16.520
no matter how far apart we are.

654
41:18.790 --> 41:22.360
Yes. I understand that well.

655
41:23.910 --> 41:27.230
I am blessed to have met you, Master Seki.

656
41:34.250 --> 41:35.670
Iroha.

657
41:41.590 --> 41:44.840
I have a gift for you as thanks for these rice balls.

658
41:45.810 --> 41:50.210
While theorizing the circumference ratio, I came up with a certain question.

659
41:50.210 --> 41:53.480
A new question of yours, Master Seki?

660
41:55.570 --> 41:57.750
I have been summoned

661
41:59.460 --> 42:01.380
by the leader of Kofu.

662
42:07.140 --> 42:12.020
The day I leave, I will post my gift to you at the Hachiman shrine.

663
42:13.160 --> 42:17.570
It is because I believe in you, that I will hold nothing back.

664
42:18.270 --> 42:19.850
I will leave the answer a blank.

665
42:19.850 --> 42:21.470
[Hachiman Shrine]

666
42:21.470 --> 42:24.180
Compete with mathematicians

667
42:25.360 --> 42:27.010
from all over Japan.

668
42:30.510 --> 42:31.780
Yes, Master Seki.

669
42:33.800 --> 42:35.660
I will solve your equation.

670
42:35.660 --> 42:39.140
I will answer whatever question you give me.

671
42:39.140 --> 42:40.860
It is a promise.

672
42:42.140 --> 42:46.550
Mathematics will always tie us together.

673
42:53.340 --> 42:55.600
No matter how far apart we are.

674
43:31.870 --> 43:33.820
Ms. Nashiki?

675
43:42.860 --> 43:46.070
Ms. Nashiki! Step back!

676
43:46.070 --> 43:48.940
- Ikuru? - Step back!

677
43:58.650 --> 44:00.700
No...

678
44:01.820 --> 44:03.820
How?

679
44:05.130 --> 44:07.390
How could I have forgotten?

680
44:07.390 --> 44:10.350
I made such an important promise...

681
44:10.940 --> 44:13.650
Promise? What promise?

682
44:13.650 --> 44:16.180
Ikuru, sorry. I have to go.

683
44:16.180 --> 44:18.600
Go where?

684
44:18.600 --> 44:20.400
Wait!

685
44:35.040 --> 44:37.410
Why would you try to go alone?

686
44:39.740 --> 44:43.410
Ms. Nashiki, you know nothing about this modern era.

687
44:46.130 --> 44:50.260
Why do you think I'm here for you?

688
44:54.610 --> 44:57.220
[Afterschool Club]

689
44:59.070 --> 45:00.810
See you!

690
45:14.810 --> 45:16.240
Naoya.

691
45:16.960 --> 45:18.710
Dad!

692
45:20.690 --> 45:23.110
- School's finished? - Yup.

693
45:24.440 --> 45:28.140
Dad's still got work, so get yourself some dinner, alright?

694
45:29.030 --> 45:31.130
- Dad. - Yeah?

695
45:31.130 --> 45:33.740
I'm not gonna go to school anymore.

696
45:34.640 --> 45:37.360
Why not? Are they bullying you again?

697
45:37.360 --> 45:41.200
No. I don't wanna be in Class 1 anymore.

698
45:41.200 --> 45:43.750
I wanna join Class 3.

699
45:43.750 --> 45:45.530
Class 3?

700
45:45.530 --> 45:49.930
Yeah. Class 3's teacher is super cool!

701
45:49.930 --> 45:52.400
Her name is Ms. Nashiki!

702
46:00.760 --> 46:04.340
If she's so great, Dad would love to meet her.

703
46:04.340 --> 46:05.710
Yeah!
